<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <AssemblyName>klee</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>KleeMod</RootNamespace>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
    <CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies>false</CopyLocalLockFileAssemblies>
    <ProduceReferenceAssembly>false</ProduceReferenceAssembly>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- THE ELEMENT PORT's switch (KleeMod.Elements.TriggerRules.SwirlPays),
       defaulted on by Directory.Build.props. It switches the shared reaction
       layer, not a kit. The prototype surface and the four kit arms that used
       to sit here are the only build since legacy cleanup stage 5: the
       shipped kits, their opt-out (ShippedKits) and the arm properties are
       gone. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(SwirlPays)' == 'true'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);SWIRL_PAYS</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- THE TEYVAT RUN FRAME ARM (R272; the frame packet
       review/active/teyvat-run-frame-2026-09-14.md sec.4, and the decompile
       read review/records/teyvat-spike-zone-read-2026-09-14.md sec.7).

           dotnet build ... -p:TeyvatFrame=true

       A SEVENTH property, on exactly the terms the second through sixth have:
       it gates an ARM and not a compilation unit. Everything the arm owns
       lives under Teyvat/**, and every one of those files reads
       `TeyvatFrame.Enabled` before it does anything: the Harmony postfixes
       return unchanged on the flag-off path, and the two dressing acts are
       never published into `ModelDb.Acts`.

       COMPILED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS ON PURPOSE, unlike Cards/Prototype/**. The
       acceptance condition of this arm is a statement about what the act list
       CONTAINS ; the base four with the flag off, two dressings standing in
       their place with it on ; and a pin that could only be compiled on one
       side of the switch could not say the first half. `TeyvatFrame.Enabled`
       is a settable static for that reason, exactly as the five arms above.

       WHAT IT COSTS WITH THE FLAG OFF, disclosed rather than assumed: the two
       `ActModel` subclasses and the one `EventModel` subclass are visible to
       `ModelDb`'s reflection walk (`ReflectionHelper.GetSubtypesInMods`), so
       they are constructed once at boot and hold a `ModelId`. They are
       reachable from NOTHING: `ModelDb.Acts` is a hardcoded four-element list
       this arm's postfix declines to touch with the flag off, and
       `ModelDb.AllEvents` is `Acts.SelectMany(a => a.AllEvents)` concatenated
       with the shared pool, so an unpublished act's events are not in it.

       THE ARM IS OFF ON EVERY CALIBRATION DEPLOY (frame packet sec.5): a
       dressing's event pool, were it ever to differ in LENGTH from the base
       zone's, would move the `UpFront` rng and with it the Klee calibration
       seed's whole map. The pools are equal by construction and pinned equal
       by `TeyvatFrameTests`; the flag staying off is the second belt. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(TeyvatFrame)' == 'true'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);TEYVAT_FRAME</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- THE WORKSHOP RELEASE BUILD (2026-10-16; ReleaseVariant.cs,
       docs/current/operations/workshop.md). Both off unless named, so dev
       deploys, seat deploys and dotnet test are unchanged. Only
       tools/package_workshop.py names them.

           -p:WorkshopRelease=true        play telemetry writes only when
                                          GITS_TELEMETRY_FEED is set
           -p:GitsKits=klee+kokomi+...    the kits that ship ('+'-separated,
                                          since ';' and ',' split -p: values);
                                          empty ships every kit -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(WorkshopRelease)' == 'true'">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);WORKSHOP_RELEASE</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- The same fact as metadata, so the packager can read it back off the
       built dll before it ships one. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(WorkshopRelease)' == 'true'">
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Reflection.AssemblyMetadataAttribute">
      <_Parameter1>GitsWorkshopRelease</_Parameter1>
      <_Parameter2>true</_Parameter2>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(GitsKits)' != ''">
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Reflection.AssemblyMetadataAttribute">
      <_Parameter1>GitsKits</_Parameter1>
      <_Parameter2>$(GitsKits)</_Parameter2>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(GitsVariant)' != ''">
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Reflection.AssemblyMetadataAttribute">
      <_Parameter1>GitsVariant</_Parameter1>
      <_Parameter2>$(GitsVariant)</_Parameter2>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- OPT-IN RUN STATS (2026-10-16; RunStats/RunStatsHook.cs,
       docs/current/operations/workshop.md). Compiled in ONLY when an
       endpoint is named:

           -p:GitsTelemetryEndpoint=https://.../v1/run

       tools/package_workshop.py passes it for a beta package given a
       telemetry endpoint, and for nothing else. Every other build
       (dev, seat, dotnet test, the public package) compiles no RunStats file
       at all: no uploader, no setting, no install id. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(GitsTelemetryEndpoint)' != ''">
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);GITS_RUN_STATS</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(GitsTelemetryEndpoint)' != ''">
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Reflection.AssemblyMetadataAttribute">
      <_Parameter1>GitsTelemetryEndpoint</_Parameter1>
      <_Parameter2>$(GitsTelemetryEndpoint)</_Parameter2>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(GitsTelemetryEndpoint)' == ''">
    <Compile Remove="RunStats/**" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- Reference the game assembly + Harmony directly. Private=false: the game
       loads these from its own data folder, we must not ship copies. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Reference Include="sts2">
      <HintPath>$(GameDataDir)\sts2.dll</HintPath>
      <Private>false</Private>
    </Reference>
    <Reference Include="0Harmony">
      <HintPath>$(GameDataDir)\0Harmony.dll</HintPath>
      <Private>false</Private>
    </Reference>
    <Reference Include="GodotSharp">
      <HintPath>$(GameDataDir)\GodotSharp.dll</HintPath>
      <Private>false</Private>
    </Reference>
    <!-- BaseLib is a Workshop mod loaded before us (see manifest dependencies).
         Needed for CustomCardModel.CustomPortrait, which accepts a Texture2D
         object and so lets us ship loose PNGs instead of building a .pck. -->
    <Reference Include="BaseLib">
      <HintPath>$(BaseLibDll)</HintPath>
      <Private>false</Private>
    </Reference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
